  "recipeCuisine": "Japan",
  "name": "Oyakodon - Chicken & Egg Rice Bowl",
  "text": "Oyakodon - Chicken & Egg Rice Bowl\n\nPreparation time:\n\nCooking time:\n\nYield: 2\n\nIngredients\n\n6 tbsp dashi,\n\n2 tbsp soy sauce,\n\n1 tbsp mirin,\n\n1 tbsp sake,\n\n1 tbsp sugar,\n\n150g chicken thigh filet (diced),\n\n1 small onion (sliced),\n\n4 eggs,\n\nchopped mitsuba (or coriander, or spring onion) to garnish,\n\n1 cup cooked Japanese rice.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Heat the dashi in a small saucepan over medium heat until it is simmering, then add the soy sauce, mirin, sake and sugar and stir until the sugar has dissolved.\n\n2. Then add the chicken and onion and cook, uncovered, for 3 to 4 minutes, or until the onions have wilted and the chicken is cooked through.  While this is cooking, gently beat the eggs very well.\n\n3. Pour the cooked onion and chicken mixture into a frying pan and heat it over medium-heat until it is simmering. Pour the beaten eggs into the center of the skillet and cook until the edges of the omelet begin to set. Simmer for 3 to 4 minutes, then garnish, and cook for an additional minute.\n\n4. Divide the rice among 2 bowls and then place one quarter of the omelet over the rice in each bowl.  Pour any seasoned broth that may remain in the pan over the omelets and serve.",
  "recipeYield": "2",
  "recipeIngredient": [
    "6 tbsp dashi,",
    "2 tbsp soy sauce,",
    "1 tbsp mirin,",
    "1 tbsp sake,",
    "1 tbsp sugar,",
    "150g chicken thigh filet (diced),",
    "1 small onion (sliced),",
    "4 eggs,",
    "chopped mitsuba (or coriander, or spring onion) to garnish,",
    "1 cup cooked Japanese rice."
  ],
